
  claim 1 · a bonded market can be drained through its own curve
      bonded with 1000000 / 1000000, offsets 6368600 / 6368600
      after 3 cycles: reserves 1513644 / 524347
      the accomplice is -513644 base, 475652 quote
  ○ refuted     a bonded market can be drained through the curve
      the accomplice ended -513644 base / 475652 quote — profit on both sides is what the claim needs and it did not happen
  ○ refuted     deposit re-anchors the curve while bonded
      the offsets did not move

  claim 2 · the whole supply can be minted for free once a verifier exists
      supply 2 → 2; the contract took 1 × the mint price for 1 tokens
  ○ refuted     cloneWithKernel issues supply without payment
      no clone succeeded

  claim 3 · a session key that nobody can ever revoke
  ○ refuted     a session may be granted an expiry nobody can outlive
      grantSession refused 2^64-1; the expiry is capped like every other promise here
      the token now owned by its own Reach: false
  ○ refuted     a session key outlives every way of revoking it
      the token could not be moved into its own account

  claim 4 · a guarded token that sets bit 255 escapes the seal
      execute(address,uint256,bytes,uint8) reverted: revert data=0x620a8bcf000000000000000000000
  ○ refuted     a token setting bit 255 walks out of a sealed vault
      the seal refused the call

  claim 5 · an asset unreadable at snapshot is exempt from its own drain
      execute(address,uint256,bytes,uint8) reverted: revert data=0xbba4bf62f2d5d56b0000000000000
      unmeasurable() reported 1 asset(s) before the call
  ○ refuted     blind at snapshot means exempt for the whole call
      the seal refused it

  claim 6 · a token hook re-anchors the curve inside somebody else's swap
      quoted 97073, received 97073
      offsets 3184300/3184300 → 3184300/3184300
  ○ refuted     a trade moved the curve it was trading against
      the offsets did not move

  claim 7 · a revoked key remembers everything it was ever allowed
      revert
  ○ refuted     a re-granted key resurrects every permission it ever had
      the old allowlist did not survive the revoke

  claim 8 · a sealed vault swaps a valuable NFT for a worthless one
      control (count only, no identity list): swap SUCCEEDED
      execute(address,uint256,bytes,uint8) reverted: revert data=0x2c69273100000000000
      the vault's count is still 1; token #1 owner 0x512e8a17 → 0x512e8a17
  ○ refuted     the seal protects how many NFTs, not which
      the control swapped freely with only the collection guarded, and this one was refused with the piece guarded — so a count is blind to identity and the identity list is what sees it

  claim 9 · the anchored offsets truncate at uint112
      rBase 2116069768159922759309664, MAX_RESERVE/8 649037107316853453566312041152511
      offsets should be 16928558145279382074477312, are 13476401925503284084939526
  ○ refuted     the anchored offsets truncate silently at uint112
      the reserve could not be driven high enough, or the cast held

  claim 10 · standing custody granted under a selector nobody listed
      execute(address,uint256,bytes,uint8) reverted: revert data=0xbba4bf6287517c45000
  ○ refuted     an approval under an unlisted selector goes through a seal
      the unlisted word was refused too

  claim 11 · a guarded token can shut a sealed vault for the length of its seal
      benign calls: 0/3 before arming, 0/3 after; escapes: 0
  ○ refuted     a guarded token can shut the account and leave no way out
      an escape was available:

  claim 12 · an attestation signature is replayable forever
      attestationDigest(purpose:string, payload:bytes32, deadline:uint64)
  ○ refuted     an attestation carries no nonce and no expiry
      the struct is purpose:string, payload:bytes32, deadline:uint64

  claim 13 · trading past the cap locks the holder out of their own market
      rBase 1000000010000000000000000000 vs cap 1000000000000000000000000000; quote-only deposit accepted
  ○ refuted     trading past maxDeposit locks the holder out of deposit entirely
      deposit still worked

  none of the 15 claims reproduced
